    box c2 "Приве́т! Как дела́?" #2f6b8f x 570 y 395 width 420 height 86 radius 22 font_size 44 hidden true
    box c3 "Хорошо́, спаси́бо!" #2f6b8f x 420 y 245 width 400 height 86 radius 22 font_size 44 hidden true
    text c1_en "hi, Masha!" #8f887c x 420 y 477 font_size 34 hidden true
    text c2_en "hi! how are things?" #8f887c x 570 y 327 font_size 34 hidden true
    text c3_en "good, thanks!" #8f887c x 420 y 177 font_size 34 hidden true
    group street members ["c1","c2","c3","c1_en","c2_en","c3_en"] hidden true
    box s1 "Здра́вствуйте!" #8a5fa8 x 420 y 520 width 380 height 86 radius 22 font_size 44 hidden true
    box s2 "Здра́вствуйте!" #8a5fa8 x 590 y 260 width 380 height 86 radius 22 font_size 44 hidden true
    text s1_en "hello" #8f887c x 420 y 452 font_size 34 hidden true
    text s2_en "hello" #8f887c x 590 y 192 font_size 34 hidden true
    group shop members ["s1","s2","s1_en","s2_en","counter"] hidden true
    box h_f "Close" #2f6b8f width 300 height 100 radius 14 icon ["people hugging","handshake"] font_size 36 in board hidden true
    box h_s "Polite" #8a5fa8 width 300 height 100 radius 14 icon ["handshake","person"] font_size 36 in board hidden true
    box w_privet "приве́т" #2f6b8f width 300 height 100 radius 14 font_size 46 in board hidden true
    box w_zdr "здра́вствуйте" #8a5fa8 width 300 height 100 radius 14 font_size 40 in board hidden true
    box w_ty "ты" #2f6b8f width 300 height 100 radius 14 font_size 46 in board hidden true
    box w_vy "вы" #8a5fa8 width 300 height 100 radius 14 font_size 46 in board hidden true
    box w_poka "пока́" #2f6b8f width 300 height 100 radius 14 font_size 46 in board hidden true
    box w_dosv "до свида́ния" #8a5fa8 width 300 height 100 radius 14 font_size 40 in board hidden true
    grid board gap 20 columns 2 fit.h 455 fit.w 530 fit.x 235 fit.y 175 hidden true
    icon granny size 140 set twemoji x 870 y 215 or ["grandmother"] icon_look picture of "old woman" hidden true
    text granny_name "Grandma" #8f887c x 870 y 120 font_size 30 hidden true
    group granny_g members ["granny","granny_name"] hidden true
    text note_a "здра" #8a5fa8 x 375 y 235 font_size 48 hidden true
    text note_v "в" #b5482e x 470 y 235 font_size 48 hidden true
    text note_c "ствуйте" #8a5fa8 x 600 y 235 font_size 48 hidden true
    mark note_x around note_v kind strike hidden true
    text note2 "ZDRAST-vuy-tye" #8f887c x 500 y 180 font_size 34 hidden true
    group note members ["note_a","note_v","note_c","note_x","note2"] hidden true
    text split_a "здра́вствуй" #8a5fa8 x 440 y 235 font_size 48 hidden true
    text split_b "+ те" #b5482e x 640 y 235 font_size 48 hidden true
    group split members ["split_a","split_b"] hidden true
    box ask_q "?" #2f6b8f x 420 y 330 width 300 height 110 radius 24 font_size 56 hidden true
    box bye_a "Пока́, Ма́ша!" #2f6b8f x 420 y 330 width 360 height 96 radius 24 font_size 46 hidden true
    box bye_b "Пока́!" #2f6b8f x 600 y 215 width 220 height 96 radius 24 font_size 46 hidden true

    card title "Привет or здравствуйте?"

A: How do you say hello in Russian? There are two everyday words, and the one you pick tells people how close you are.
    draw tom tom_name masha masha_name

A: Masha and I are old friends, so listen to how we greet each other in the street.
    draw tag_street

A: Привет, Маша!
    draw c1

B: Привет! Как дела?
    draw c2

A: Хорошо, спасибо!
    draw c3

A: Привет is hi; как дела asks how things are; and хорошо, спасибо means good, thanks.
    draw c1_en c2_en c3_en

    erase street

B: But I'd never say привет to a shop assistant, or to my teacher.
    highlight masha effect circle

A: So now Masha stands behind a shop counter, and I walk in.
    draw tag_shop counter

A: Здравствуйте!
    draw s1

B: Здравствуйте!
    draw s2 s1_en s2_en

    erase shop tag_shop

A: Two hellos, then: привет for friends, and здравствуйте for strangers, older people, or a teacher.
    draw h_f h_s w_privet w_zdr

A: Russian splits the word you the same way.
    draw w_ty w_vy

B: Ты is for one person I'm close to. Вы is for someone I'd greet with здравствуйте, or for more than one person.
    blocking false

    highlight masha effect circle duration 0.6

    highlight w_ty duration 2

    highlight w_vy duration 4

    highlight tom effect circle duration 0.6

A: Listen to the end of здравствуйте: that те is the вы ending, so the polite hello has its вы built in.
    draw split

    erase split

    draw granny_g

    ask "Which do you call her, ты or вы? Tap the word on the board." choose ["w_ty","w_vy"] answer w_vy
        intro: Your friend's grandmother opens the door.
        right: Вы: she is older and new to you, so it's вы, and здравствуйте.
        wrong: Is she one of your close friends?

    erase granny_g

B: Now, здравствуйте looks like a mouthful.
    highlight masha w_zdr

    quiz "How do you think Russians say it?"
        right: Zdrast-vuy-tye: the first в is written, but nobody says it.
        wrong: Try saying all of zdrav-stv: is there an easier way?
        * zdrav-stvuy-tye
        + zdrast-vuy-tye

B: Здравствуйте.
    draw note

    erase note

A: Goodbye splits the same way.
    highlight tom effect circle

    highlight masha effect circle duration 0.6

B: Пока to a friend; до свидания, until we meet again, to everyone else.
    draw w_poka w_dosv

    hide board speakers

    cards match size 1.7 y 530
        * "Meet a friend" icon ["people hugging","handshake"] match Приве́т!
        * "Meet Grandma" icon ["old woman","grandmother"] match Здра́вствуйте!
        * "Leave a friend" icon ["waving hand"] match Пока́!
        * "Leave a shop" icon ["convenience store","shopping cart"] match "До свида́ния!"

    ask "Match each moment to what you say." on match store m stage own
        intro: Now from memory, with the board put away.
        right: Привет and пока for a friend; здравствуйте and до свидания for the rest.
        wrong: You got {m} on the first try.

    erase match

    show speakers

    draw ask_q

    ask "Type how you greet me, your friend Masha." answer ["привет"] translit true reveal Приве́т! reveal_at ask_q keys АБВГДЕЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУХЫЯ
        right: Привет: I'm a friend, so it's ты, and the short hello.
        wrong: I'm a friend: the short one, six letters.

    erase ask_q

    show board

A: So Russian has two ways of talking to people, ты and вы, close and polite, and every hello and goodbye picks one of them.
    highlight w_ty w_vy

    quiz "Your new boss is 25, the same age as you, and you have just met. Which hello?" reveal Здра́вствуйте! reveal_at.x 700 reveal_at.y 150
        right: Здравствуйте: a boss you have just met gets вы, whatever her age.
        wrong: It isn't about age: have you just met, and is it work?
        * Привет!
        + Здравствуйте!

B: And when you're not sure, start with здравствуйте: a Russian will tell you when it's time for привет.
    highlight masha w_zdr

    hide board

A: Пока, Маша!
    draw bye_a

B: Пока!
    draw bye_b

